1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:02,202
No one would deliberately kill Joyce.

2
00:00:02,202 --> 00:00:03,237
Right, Director Phil?

3
00:00:03,237 --> 00:00:06,372
I know you think I was behind what happened.

4
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:07,745
I didn't say anything like that.

5
00:00:07,746 --> 00:00:11,620
Maybe the police are just overly suspicious
of everyone.

6
00:00:11,622 --> 00:00:14,279
It's just a simple case of neglect.

7
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,032
There's no one to blame but me.

8
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:19,887
I insisted on working with her.

9
00:00:19,887 --> 00:00:22,056
<i>I'm recording myself right now.</i>

10
00:00:22,056 --> 00:00:24,390
<i>This is about the suspect, Lando.</i>

11
00:00:24,391 --> 00:00:27,660
<i>And his boss, Congressman Ramon dela Peña.</i>

12
00:00:27,661 --> 00:00:29,296
Put your hands up.

13
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:32,242
Freeze! You're under arrest.

14
00:00:32,242 --> 00:00:36,145
Tell me.
You have nothing to do with it. Right?

15
00:00:57,434 --> 00:00:59,124
Joyce...

16
00:01:02,531 --> 00:01:04,799
What kind of life is this?

17
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:16,419
I don't know if this is a curse.

18
00:01:20,886 --> 00:01:30,471
I was given a typewriter to change our lives.

19
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:38,509
But things only got worse...

20
00:01:43,346 --> 00:01:45,470
And it led to this tragedy.

21
00:01:56,726 --> 00:02:02,665
I'm tired of blaming the world.

22
00:02:05,066 --> 00:02:10,581
I'm tired of blaming the typewriter.

23
00:02:14,644 --> 00:02:16,471
Because I know...

24
00:02:20,249 --> 00:02:22,644
from the beginning...

25
00:02:24,754 --> 00:02:28,290
that there's no one to blame but me.

26
00:02:30,227 --> 00:02:32,118
Joyce, sorry.

27
00:02:33,497 --> 00:02:35,321
Sorry.

28
00:02:41,871 --> 00:02:44,321
I love you so much.

29
00:02:49,746 --> 00:02:52,212
I love you so much...

30
00:02:55,244 --> 00:02:57,720
Ever since the beginning...

31
00:02:59,081 --> 00:03:02,551
Even back in our old world...

32
00:03:04,449 --> 00:03:06,268
I love you.

33
00:03:08,152 --> 00:03:10,907
I love you so much too.

34
00:03:14,327 --> 00:03:16,295
So much.

35
00:03:19,442 --> 00:03:24,020
Until this present time,
I still love you so much.

36
00:03:33,657 --> 00:03:37,842
I'm also happy working with you.

37
00:03:39,462 --> 00:03:43,778
Wait, where is this conversation headed?

38
00:03:43,778 --> 00:03:45,519
I love you.

39
00:03:51,741 --> 00:03:56,762
If I will be given a chance...

40
00:04:00,837 --> 00:04:05,989
To change everything again...

41
00:04:08,921 --> 00:04:11,473
I would do the right thing.

42
00:04:14,998 --> 00:04:16,824
Even though it hurts.

43
00:04:20,636 --> 00:04:22,904
I would stay away from you.

44
00:04:27,998 --> 00:04:31,029
I will let you be happy.

45
00:04:32,707 --> 00:04:35,451
Even if I'm not the one you're with.

46
00:04:42,826 --> 00:04:45,623
I love you so much, Joyce.

47
00:04:52,537 --> 00:04:53,804
Hey!

48
00:04:53,804 --> 00:04:55,873
Hey, stop!

49
00:04:55,873 --> 00:04:57,407
Stop it!

50
00:05:07,285 --> 00:05:09,387
Move!

51
00:05:09,387 --> 00:05:10,859
Intoy?

52
00:05:12,990 --> 00:05:14,458
Move!

53
00:05:14,458 --> 00:05:15,826
Move! I'm going to hit you.

54
00:05:15,826 --> 00:05:17,428
- I said move.
- You're so stubborn.

55
00:05:17,428 --> 00:05:19,297
Sir, wait, wait.

56
00:05:19,297 --> 00:05:21,132
- What's going on here?
- Hey, Bro.

57
00:05:21,132 --> 00:05:23,699
They want to arrest me,
but I'm not doing anything wrong.

58
00:05:23,699 --> 00:05:27,106
What are you talking about?
You've been told not to stay there.

59
00:05:27,106 --> 00:05:29,173
You're stubborn.

60
00:05:30,110 --> 00:05:31,430
What happened?

61
00:05:31,431 --> 00:05:34,767
Bro, I was just scavenging
for junk I could sell.

62
00:05:34,768 --> 00:05:36,746
You heard him, Sir.

63
00:05:36,747 --> 00:05:40,183
Sir, I'll take care of him. I know Intoy.

64
00:05:40,184 --> 00:05:43,421
Fine, just make sure
he won't return to our neighborhood.

65
00:05:43,421 --> 00:05:45,778
Yes, Sir. I got it.

66
00:05:57,301 --> 00:05:58,755
Hey, Bro.

67
00:05:59,503 --> 00:06:00,836
Is that really you, Bro?

68
00:06:00,836 --> 00:06:02,825
"Hey Bro", my foot.

69
00:06:02,825 --> 00:06:05,775
I've been looking for you, Intoy.
Where were you?

70
00:06:05,775 --> 00:06:07,311
Thank you, Bro.

71
00:06:07,311 --> 00:06:10,356
I would have been arrested
if it wasn't for you.

72
00:06:11,616 --> 00:06:13,351
What are you doing here, anyway?

73
00:06:13,351 --> 00:06:14,903
Why are you here?

74
00:06:16,187 --> 00:06:18,388
I visited Joyce.

75
00:06:20,324 --> 00:06:22,099
Savana.

76
00:06:23,194 --> 00:06:25,654
Oh, yeah.

77
00:06:25,654 --> 00:06:28,799
I broke down and cried when I saw the news.

78
00:06:28,799 --> 00:06:31,401
May she rest in peace.

79
00:06:33,369 --> 00:06:37,673
Intoy, I'd love to talk to you more,

80
00:06:37,673 --> 00:06:39,642
but I have an important thing to do.

81
00:06:39,642 --> 00:06:41,436
What is it, Bro?

82
00:06:42,584 --> 00:06:45,850
Something that I should have done before.

83
00:06:46,703 --> 00:06:50,170
I need to do what's right.

84
00:06:54,490 --> 00:06:56,893
Okay, Bro.

85
00:06:56,893 --> 00:06:59,975
I'll just give you something before you go.

86
00:07:01,798 --> 00:07:03,900
Sorry, Bro. This is all I can give you.

87
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,501
Please accept it.

88
00:07:05,501 --> 00:07:08,404
Intoy, no. You need this more.

89
00:07:08,404 --> 00:07:11,541
Come on, Bro. Please accept it.

90
00:07:11,541 --> 00:07:15,678
So I can be a good friend to you too somehow.

91
00:07:15,678 --> 00:07:17,680
Go on, Bro. Don't say no.

92
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:18,714
Thank you, Intoy.

93
00:07:18,714 --> 00:07:20,016
Here, Bro.

94
00:07:20,016 --> 00:07:22,084
You might choke.

95
00:07:24,253 --> 00:07:26,200
Intoy, what's this?

96
00:07:47,141 --> 00:07:51,685
Where did you get this typewriter?

97
00:07:54,417 --> 00:07:56,740
I've been looking for this.

98
00:07:57,887 --> 00:07:59,187
What are you going to do, Bro?

99
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,796
I need to write something.

100
00:08:01,796 --> 00:08:03,726
Is that the important thing you have to do?

101
00:08:03,726 --> 00:08:05,428
No, no, no.

102
00:08:05,428 --> 00:08:08,429
This is different.
This is more important than that.

103
00:08:08,429 --> 00:08:10,433
Is that the "right thing"
you're talking about?

104
00:08:10,433 --> 00:08:13,734
Intoy, I don't care
whether it's wrong or right.

105
00:08:13,734 --> 00:08:15,881
Bro, even if there's a price to pay?

106
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,595
What are you talking about?

107
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:33,499
- Bro, don't use that. That's mine.
- Intoy, stop!

108
00:08:33,499 --> 00:08:35,455
- Bro, that's mine!
- Intoy, this is mine!

109
00:08:35,455 --> 00:08:37,460
- You just found it. This is mine!
- Bro, don't!

110
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:38,895
I've been looking for this, Intoy.

111
00:08:38,895 --> 00:08:40,763
Stop. Bro, don't do it.

112
00:08:40,763 --> 00:08:42,298
- This is mine!
- Bro, that's mine.

113
00:08:42,298 --> 00:08:43,165
- Intoy!
- Bro!

114
00:08:43,165 --> 00:08:45,005
This is mine.

115
00:08:46,286 --> 00:08:48,922
Bro, you don't know what you're doing.

116
00:08:50,907 --> 00:08:52,909
Bro...

117
00:08:52,909 --> 00:08:55,215
Please shut up, Intoy.

118
00:08:56,598 --> 00:08:57,942
Bro!

119
00:08:59,782 --> 00:09:02,608
Bro, what are you writing?

120
00:09:02,608 --> 00:09:10,192
<i>For the second time,
I brought tragedy to your life, my love.</i>

121
00:09:10,192 --> 00:09:12,495
Bro, I said stop it!

122
00:09:12,495 --> 00:09:14,086
Bro!

123
00:09:18,067 --> 00:09:20,636
Bro, it can't correct all your mistakes.

124
00:09:20,636 --> 00:09:22,805
What do you mean, Intoy?

125
00:09:22,805 --> 00:09:25,675
<i>Sorry, I was stubborn.</i>

126
00:09:25,675 --> 00:09:27,752
<i>I love you so much.</i>

127
00:09:27,752 --> 00:09:30,646
<i>Sorry for getting stuck
in my messy life again.</i>

128
00:09:30,646 --> 00:09:32,648
<i>I feel like I killed you.</i>

129
00:09:32,648 --> 00:09:35,217
<i>I want to bring your life back.</i>

130
00:09:35,217 --> 00:09:36,819
<i>I wish you didn't know</i>

131
00:09:36,819 --> 00:09:39,956
<i>about Congressman Ramon dela Peña's
evil doings.</i>

132
00:09:39,956 --> 00:09:42,058
<i>And you didn't get dragged
into all this mess.</i>

133
00:09:42,058 --> 00:09:44,399
Brace yourself, Bro!
It always comes with a price!

134
00:09:45,561 --> 00:09:49,689
<i>You could have been alive today, Joyce.</i>

135
00:09:49,689 --> 00:09:51,801
No one should use the typewriter!

136
00:09:51,801 --> 00:09:53,235
It has a curse.

137
00:09:56,673 --> 00:09:58,223
Intoy!

138
00:10:03,679 --> 00:10:04,981
<i>Joyce, hang in there.</i>

139
00:10:04,981 --> 00:10:06,382
<i>4:46 AM, time of death.</i>

140
00:10:06,382 --> 00:10:09,685
<i>The suspect, Congressman Ramon dela Peña.</i>

141
00:10:09,685 --> 00:10:11,715
<i>I love you, Joyce.</i>

142
00:10:34,734 --> 00:10:36,133
[Write Here Waiting]

143
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:37,580
I know.

144
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:39,550
True.

145
00:10:41,814 --> 00:10:45,042
- Sir Liam.
- Sir Liam, let's take a picture.

146
00:10:45,042 --> 00:10:46,493
This is it.

147
00:10:53,049 --> 00:10:56,285
Sir Liam, congrats!

148
00:10:57,453 --> 00:10:59,035
Liam, this is it.

149
00:10:59,035 --> 00:11:00,970
Everyone is so excited.

150
00:11:02,038 --> 00:11:03,706
Oh, boy. I'm so excited.

151
00:11:03,706 --> 00:11:06,208
We're about to see it.

152
00:11:06,208 --> 00:11:10,351
My God. You really are something, Phil.
This will be a blockbuster.

153
00:11:11,406 --> 00:11:14,851
Sir Liam, congratulations.

154
00:11:37,139 --> 00:11:40,242
Hi, Director Phil. Congratulations!

155
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:43,901
Congrats to us.

156
00:11:46,387 --> 00:11:48,002
Love.

157
00:11:50,502 --> 00:11:53,656
What's up with your face? We should smile.

158
00:11:53,656 --> 00:11:55,737
It's your big day.

159
00:11:57,953 --> 00:11:59,987
What's happening?

160
00:12:02,665 --> 00:12:05,167
Please understand my boyfriend.

161
00:12:05,167 --> 00:12:06,635
It seems that it hasn't sunk in yet

162
00:12:06,635 --> 00:12:09,247
that we're about to premiere the film
we all worked hard for.

163
00:12:09,247 --> 00:12:10,639
Congrats.

164
00:12:10,639 --> 00:12:12,808
Social media is exploding.

165
00:12:12,808 --> 00:12:15,945
So I'm sure this will be a hit.

166
00:12:15,945 --> 00:12:17,113
Congrats.

167
00:12:17,113 --> 00:12:18,681
Thanks to Joyce.

168
00:12:18,681 --> 00:12:21,839
Despite what happened to us in the past,

169
00:12:21,839 --> 00:12:24,009
she still trusted me.

170
00:12:24,887 --> 00:12:28,791
Love... I know how you feel.

171
00:12:28,791 --> 00:12:33,195
That's how I am
every time Escale releases a new issue.

172
00:12:33,195 --> 00:12:37,700
Don't worry.
All you have to do is smile and project.

173
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:39,885
Everything's going to be alright.

174
00:12:40,669 --> 00:12:43,405
- Joyce is here!
- Joyce...

175
00:12:44,948 --> 00:12:46,806
Joyce.

176
00:12:49,678 --> 00:12:51,711
Oh my god.

177
00:12:54,817 --> 00:12:56,252
Joyce.

178
00:12:56,252 --> 00:12:58,751
Oh my God.

179
00:13:16,372 --> 00:13:19,441
<i>Your story has once again changed, Liam.</i>

180
00:13:19,441 --> 00:13:22,112
<i>I'm sure there is a price to pay.</i>

181
00:13:28,050 --> 00:13:30,419
Thank you.

182
00:13:30,419 --> 00:13:32,721
Hello.

183
00:13:32,721 --> 00:13:34,323
Congratulations.

184
00:13:34,323 --> 00:13:35,706
Joyce.

185
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:05,454
Joyce.

186
00:14:05,454 --> 00:14:06,689
Hi!

187
00:14:08,691 --> 00:14:10,926
- Hi, guys. Good evening.
- Hello.

188
00:14:10,926 --> 00:14:13,542
- You're so beautiful.
- Thank you.

189
00:14:14,581 --> 00:14:18,604
So, Joyce, we have a few questions.
Is it okay?

190
00:14:20,003 --> 00:14:23,673
We know
you've done quite a lot of love stories.

191
00:14:23,673 --> 00:14:25,308
My question is...

192
00:14:25,308 --> 00:14:29,362
How different is this film
from the previous ones you did?

193
00:14:32,248 --> 00:14:37,054
Well, in this film,

194
00:14:37,054 --> 00:14:41,456
we showed the concept of a second chance.

195
00:14:42,358 --> 00:14:48,765
When we hear of second chance,
we think of new love.

196
00:14:48,765 --> 00:14:55,355
But for me, honestly,
a second chance means...

197
00:14:55,355 --> 00:14:59,742
a chance to love ourselves.

198
00:14:59,742 --> 00:15:04,280
Once you're whole,
that's when you can truly love.

199
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:06,049
That's very well said.

200
00:15:06,049 --> 00:15:07,784
How about in real life?

201
00:15:07,784 --> 00:15:10,900
Is it still self-love for you?

202
00:15:16,192 --> 00:15:17,834
Sorry, it's a bit awkward for me

203
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:21,735
because Joyce usually is the one
who answers those kinds of questions,

204
00:15:21,736 --> 00:15:23,022
but...

205
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:25,967
I guess it's time...

206
00:15:28,524 --> 00:15:30,145
that I man up.

207
00:15:43,152 --> 00:15:45,189
Oh my God!

208
00:15:53,830 --> 00:15:56,963
Girlfriend proposal!

209
00:15:57,834 --> 00:15:59,502
Girlfriend proposal.

210
00:15:59,502 --> 00:16:02,505
This is crazy, girls!

211
00:16:03,536 --> 00:16:05,904
Oh my God.

212
00:16:06,794 --> 00:16:08,620
Will you be my girlfriend?

213
00:16:09,455 --> 00:16:11,690
Oh my God.

214
00:16:14,851 --> 00:16:17,026
Yes.

215
00:16:25,762 --> 00:16:27,242
Joyce.

216
00:16:31,935 --> 00:16:33,507
Joyce...

217
00:16:38,107 --> 00:16:40,550
Should I keep waiting or...

218
00:16:43,212 --> 00:16:45,214
Are you rejecting my feelings?

219
00:16:52,388 --> 00:16:54,144
Hans...

220
00:16:55,825 --> 00:16:59,347
After everything
that happened the past week...

221
00:17:01,664 --> 00:17:08,714
I saw and realized that in the past years,

222
00:17:13,910 --> 00:17:19,355
no one else stayed by my side but you.

223
00:17:22,277 --> 00:17:26,653
You, who's waiting for me.

224
00:17:30,193 --> 00:17:35,341
You, who's putting up with my moods.

225
00:17:36,991 --> 00:17:40,769
You, who's always there when I have problems.

226
00:17:44,607 --> 00:17:46,761
It's only you.

227
00:17:50,847 --> 00:17:52,636
I'm sorry.

228
00:17:55,518 --> 00:17:58,454
I'm sorry,
I don't want to be your girlfriend.

229
00:17:58,454 --> 00:18:01,895
Oh, that hurts.

230
00:18:05,962 --> 00:18:07,540
Because...

231
00:18:11,706 --> 00:18:14,136
I want to be your wife.

232
00:18:19,575 --> 00:18:22,398
This is a lot!

233
00:18:26,562 --> 00:18:29,391
Congratulations!

234
00:18:36,492 --> 00:18:37,853
Joyce, I love you.

235
00:18:37,853 --> 00:18:39,609
I love you.

236
00:18:42,965 --> 00:18:44,934
Oh my God!

237
00:18:44,934 --> 00:18:47,437
And now it's official.

238
00:18:47,437 --> 00:18:50,940
The then-rumored
non-showbiz boyfriend of Joyce

239
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:52,809
is not just her official boyfriend now.

240
00:18:52,809 --> 00:18:54,703
He's already her fiancé!

241
00:18:55,344 --> 00:18:59,248
And, of course,
we look forward to their wedding.

242
00:18:59,248 --> 00:19:03,018
Oh, dear. I'm so thrilled.
I feel like fainting.

243
00:19:03,018 --> 00:19:04,320
My god. This is so thrilling.

244
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:06,778
I feel like fainting, friend.

245
00:19:23,706 --> 00:19:25,727
- My god, what happened?
- Love?

246
00:19:29,037 --> 00:19:30,485
Love!

247
00:20:10,987 --> 00:20:15,658
It's beautiful.
You know how to pick a good ring.

248
00:20:15,658 --> 00:20:17,527
Son!

249
00:20:17,527 --> 00:20:19,167
- Liam.
- Love.

250
00:20:19,167 --> 00:20:20,997
Are you okay now?

251
00:20:20,997 --> 00:20:23,612
We wanted to bring you to the hospital.

252
00:20:23,612 --> 00:20:28,071
But the medic said it's just over fatigue.
Why don't you sit down.

253
00:20:29,274 --> 00:20:31,040
Oh, son.

254
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:34,243
Did you know I even dressed up?

255
00:20:34,243 --> 00:20:36,279
Only to find out
I need to look after my child

256
00:20:36,279 --> 00:20:39,014
when I got to your event?

257
00:20:40,550 --> 00:20:44,220
You know,
I think it's because he's been too busy.

258
00:20:44,220 --> 00:20:46,789
You haven't had enough sleep
because you're busy preparing

259
00:20:46,789 --> 00:20:49,289
for the premiere night, right?

260
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:53,321
We'll let you sleep.
You should get some rest.

261
00:20:54,797 --> 00:20:57,733
Son, how are you?

262
00:20:57,733 --> 00:20:59,865
Do you want some medicine?

263
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:04,365
No, I'm okay.

264
00:21:06,409 --> 00:21:09,771
Liam, you missed a lot.

265
00:21:10,913 --> 00:21:16,100
Too bad you didn't see
how people applauded our film.

266
00:21:17,076 --> 00:21:20,056
I was so happy.

267
00:21:20,056 --> 00:21:24,092
So happy and overwhelmed.

268
00:21:28,589 --> 00:21:32,492
Are you happy
only because of the success of the movie, babe?

269
00:21:34,757 --> 00:21:38,474
Of course, I'm so happy
because of this too, babe.

270
00:21:43,141 --> 00:21:47,299
Oh, boy. I'm so happy for you, Joyce, Hans.

271
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:50,719
Congratulations to the both of you.

272
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:51,854
Thank you.

273
00:21:51,854 --> 00:21:53,613
Gosh.

274
00:21:54,423 --> 00:21:56,325
Me, too.

275
00:21:56,325 --> 00:21:58,861
Congrats again, guys.

276
00:21:58,861 --> 00:22:00,554
Let's celebrate?

277
00:22:01,530 --> 00:22:02,531
Cheers!

278
00:22:02,531 --> 00:22:04,100
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

279
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:06,335
Congratulations.

280
00:22:06,335 --> 00:22:08,546
Son...

281
00:22:12,022 --> 00:22:14,290
Are you okay, Liam?

282
00:22:18,878 --> 00:22:20,426
Of course.

283
00:22:22,151 --> 00:22:26,517
We're together,
and we fulfilled our dreams...

284
00:22:26,517 --> 00:22:29,099
through this movie project.

285
00:22:30,026 --> 00:22:34,272
So I don't see any reason to be...

286
00:22:34,272 --> 00:22:36,247
unhappy.

287
00:22:37,867 --> 00:22:40,669
<i>If I could have a chance...</i>

288
00:22:40,669 --> 00:22:48,692
A chance to change everything again,

289
00:22:48,692 --> 00:22:51,246
<i>I would do the right thing.</i>

290
00:22:51,881 --> 00:22:53,049
<i>Even if it hurts.</i>

291
00:22:53,049 --> 00:22:55,351
<i>I will stay away from you.</i>

292
00:22:55,351 --> 00:22:58,099
<i>I will let you be happy...</i>

293
00:22:59,989 --> 00:23:03,052
Even if you're with someone else.

294
00:23:07,930 --> 00:23:09,556
So...

295
00:23:10,848 --> 00:23:14,713
Good luck with your next movie.

296
00:23:17,874 --> 00:23:20,875
Why does it feel
like you're saying goodbye to me?

297
00:23:22,211 --> 00:23:25,014
Don't you want to work with me anymore?

298
00:23:36,459 --> 00:23:37,943
Liam...

299
00:23:39,853 --> 00:23:41,882
I'm so happy...

300
00:23:43,334 --> 00:23:47,968
that the whole world will see
the film we worked hard for...

301
00:23:54,131 --> 00:23:56,315
Except for my father.

302
00:23:59,215 --> 00:24:00,654
Why?

303
00:24:01,545 --> 00:24:03,537
What happened to Uncle Edmond?

304
00:24:04,453 --> 00:24:05,921
Are you serious?

305
00:24:05,921 --> 00:24:09,147
Are you really asking me
what happened to my father?

306
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:14,128
Are you really awake, Liam?

307
00:24:15,331 --> 00:24:17,553
I'm sorry, Joyce.

308
00:24:20,836 --> 00:24:23,670
Sorry, maybe...

309
00:24:24,964 --> 00:24:27,178
Maybe you're still confused.

310
00:24:30,303 --> 00:24:32,162
My dad...

311
00:24:35,589 --> 00:24:37,953
He became blind, remember?

312
00:24:38,768 --> 00:24:40,386
Blind?

313
00:24:41,157 --> 00:24:42,503
Yeah.

314
00:24:45,694 --> 00:24:47,862
He had...

315
00:24:49,532 --> 00:24:54,953
My father had another episode
inside the wellness center.

316
00:24:59,542 --> 00:25:03,112
I don't know what triggered it.

317
00:25:03,112 --> 00:25:10,619
And the rehab couldn't explain
why my father had access

318
00:25:10,619 --> 00:25:13,800
to their medical storage room.

319
00:25:18,037 --> 00:25:19,985
My dad...

320
00:25:22,279 --> 00:25:27,086
He overdosed on quinine.

321
00:25:28,871 --> 00:25:31,664
A malaria medicine.

322
00:25:35,678 --> 00:25:38,965
Maybe he just took whatever he grabbed.

323
00:25:42,406 --> 00:25:52,193
After a few hours, his eyesight got affected.

324
00:25:53,696 --> 00:25:56,756
The doctor said
there was nothing we could do.

325
00:26:04,607 --> 00:26:06,775
Joyce...

326
00:26:06,775 --> 00:26:08,847
It's so sad.

327
00:26:12,882 --> 00:26:15,088
It's sad because...

328
00:26:18,085 --> 00:26:21,705
Because my father was there with me...

329
00:26:24,244 --> 00:26:26,330
back in the cinema.

330
00:26:27,293 --> 00:26:29,252
He was beside me.

331
00:26:31,560 --> 00:26:34,228
But he couldn't see anything.

332
00:26:42,144 --> 00:26:44,080
It hurts.

333
00:26:48,117 --> 00:26:50,664
It hurts me because...

334
00:26:54,823 --> 00:26:58,343
no matter how many films I make...

335
00:27:03,432 --> 00:27:07,651
Even if I do my best
in my succeeding films...

336
00:27:10,657 --> 00:27:13,589
He can no longer see them.

337
00:27:21,183 --> 00:27:23,168
Joyce, I'm sorry.

338
00:27:25,821 --> 00:27:30,728
I'm sorry for what happened to Uncle Edmond.

339
00:27:40,536 --> 00:27:43,439
Hey, join us.

340
00:27:44,440 --> 00:27:45,954
Oh, sorry.

341
00:27:49,045 --> 00:27:52,501
Why do you always spend time together?

342
00:27:57,494 --> 00:28:00,356
Although...

343
00:28:00,356 --> 00:28:03,956
I feel I need to get some rest now.

344
00:28:04,993 --> 00:28:07,954
We have to be early tomorrow, Love.

345
00:28:07,954 --> 00:28:10,415
What's happening tomorrow?

346
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:15,423
Didn't Borj remind you
of your schedule tomorrow?

347
00:28:17,239 --> 00:28:20,075
We have a meeting with my dad.

348
00:28:20,075 --> 00:28:22,344
Come on.

349
00:28:22,344 --> 00:28:24,246
It's for his candidacy.

350
00:28:24,246 --> 00:28:26,081
He's running for Senate, remember?

351
00:28:26,081 --> 00:28:27,916
He hired you.

352
00:28:27,916 --> 00:28:32,295
You will do his campaign ads.

353
00:28:33,168 --> 00:28:35,295
Are you okay?

354
00:28:49,567 --> 00:29:00,666
[Edmond, Father of Joyce Trinidad]

355
00:29:00,667 --> 00:29:02,600
[Edmond Trinidad,
father of famous actress Joyce Trinidad,]

356
00:29:02,601 --> 00:29:04,520
[went blind due to drug overdose]

357
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:08,667
<i>The story behind what happened to you
isn't convincing, Uncle Edmond.</i>

358
00:29:08,667 --> 00:29:13,486
<i>I'm the only one who knows</i>

359
00:29:13,487 --> 00:29:16,885
<i>that there might be another reason
for what happened to you.</i>

360
00:29:22,371 --> 00:29:23,847
So?

361
00:29:25,274 --> 00:29:27,550
How are you feeling?

362
00:29:28,911 --> 00:29:33,706
Maybe you fainted
because you're so stressed out.

363
00:29:36,308 --> 00:29:37,895
I'm okay, Mom.

364
00:29:37,895 --> 00:29:39,761
Don't worry about me.

365
00:29:41,824 --> 00:29:44,401
But I'm happy for you, son.

366
00:29:45,394 --> 00:29:48,754
Now that you got everything you want,

367
00:29:48,754 --> 00:29:51,214
what's your next step?

368
00:29:55,015 --> 00:29:57,487
I don't want to make a mistake, Mom.

369
00:30:04,370 --> 00:30:06,120
I don't want to.

370
00:30:08,617 --> 00:30:10,786
My son...

371
00:30:10,786 --> 00:30:13,021
Come on.

372
00:30:13,021 --> 00:30:15,357
I'm just asking you about your plans.

373
00:30:15,357 --> 00:30:18,256
And you're already worried
about something else.

374
00:30:20,129 --> 00:30:25,740
Liam, son, people make mistakes.

375
00:30:27,336 --> 00:30:31,720
You're not human if you don't make mistakes.

376
00:30:34,166 --> 00:30:36,001
But, Mom...

377
00:30:37,812 --> 00:30:45,702
Whenever I try
to correct the mistakes I made,

378
00:30:45,702 --> 00:30:49,105
things don't turn out how I want them to be.

379
00:30:52,694 --> 00:30:56,231
You have to stand firm...

380
00:30:56,231 --> 00:30:59,480
especially by the decisions you make.

381
00:31:00,736 --> 00:31:07,121
You have to face the consequences
of your decision.

382
00:31:13,633 --> 00:31:15,075
Son...

383
00:31:17,519 --> 00:31:18,754
What is it, son?

384
00:31:18,754 --> 00:31:21,287
What are you looking at?

385
00:31:21,287 --> 00:31:22,925
It's nothing, Mom.

386
00:31:22,925 --> 00:31:24,827
You should get some rest.

387
00:31:24,827 --> 00:31:26,929
It's late.

388
00:31:26,929 --> 00:31:29,364
You're the one who fainted.

389
00:31:29,364 --> 00:31:31,391
You should be the one resting.

390
00:31:31,391 --> 00:31:33,121
You're so silly.

391
00:31:34,304 --> 00:31:37,684
Go on. I got this.

392
00:31:38,674 --> 00:31:40,254
Are you sure?

393
00:31:41,210 --> 00:31:43,111
Okay. Go to bed early, okay?

394
00:31:43,111 --> 00:31:44,527
I will.

395
00:31:45,366 --> 00:31:46,996
Good night, Mom.

396
00:32:06,935 --> 00:32:12,914
I'm glad you accepted my offer
to give our friendship a second chance, Liam.

397
00:32:18,714 --> 00:32:21,367
But I will make it clear to you, Liam.

398
00:32:22,398 --> 00:32:27,165
Don't use your obsession with second chances

399
00:32:27,165 --> 00:32:30,484
as a theme for my campaign series.

400
00:32:31,793 --> 00:32:35,634
Why would I need a second chance?

401
00:32:35,634 --> 00:32:38,367
I'm not doing anything wrong.

402
00:32:40,369 --> 00:32:44,340
Second chances are only for the weak.

403
00:32:44,340 --> 00:32:47,672
For people who always make mistakes.

404
00:32:48,778 --> 00:32:52,448
That's why they're asking
for a second chance.

405
00:32:52,448 --> 00:32:54,383
And that's not me.

406
00:32:55,593 --> 00:32:59,555
What we need to communicate to the voters,

407
00:32:59,555 --> 00:33:05,561
is I will continue
the good things I've started.

408
00:33:05,561 --> 00:33:09,298
And this time, we take it to the next level.

409
00:33:09,298 --> 00:33:12,802
Something that
will make people look up to me.

410
00:33:12,802 --> 00:33:17,608
We will set the bar pretty high
so no one can beat us.

411
00:33:18,774 --> 00:33:20,631
Yes, Dad.

412
00:33:20,631 --> 00:33:22,278
Don't worry.

413
00:33:22,278 --> 00:33:22,934
I'll make sure

414
00:33:22,934 --> 00:33:28,417
Liam will implement your directions
in the campaign accordingly.

415
00:33:28,417 --> 00:33:31,821
I'll take care of it. Okay?

416
00:33:42,465 --> 00:33:45,835
Sorry, I have to go. I need to do something.

417
00:33:45,835 --> 00:33:47,475
Love.

418
00:33:49,572 --> 00:33:51,420
Let's talk later.

419
00:34:03,349 --> 00:34:04,854
<i>Hans.</i>

420
00:34:04,854 --> 00:34:07,529
<i>Thank you for meeting with me.</i>

421
00:34:09,191 --> 00:34:11,604
I just want to know

422
00:34:11,604 --> 00:34:13,629
what happened to your investigation

423
00:34:13,629 --> 00:34:16,933
of the death
of a Casa Fuerte construction worker.

424
00:34:16,933 --> 00:34:18,434
Siloy?

425
00:34:18,434 --> 00:34:19,977
Liam.

426
00:34:21,304 --> 00:34:25,399
You know
that the cases I handle are confidential.

427
00:34:34,116 --> 00:34:36,385
But I'm wondering.

428
00:34:37,668 --> 00:34:40,323
Why are you interested in this case?

429
00:34:40,323 --> 00:34:42,325
What's going on, Liam?

430
00:34:44,388 --> 00:34:45,954
Because I know...

431
00:34:47,200 --> 00:34:51,139
you suspect
that Casa Fuerte is involved in Siloy's death.

432
00:34:52,034 --> 00:34:53,733
Is that right?

433
00:34:56,047 --> 00:35:00,876
Maybe that's why I don't want
to tell you anything, Liam.

434
00:35:00,876 --> 00:35:05,826
Because your family might be involved.

435
00:35:09,975 --> 00:35:12,671
What's your motive, Liam?

436
00:35:12,672 --> 00:35:14,873
What do you want?

437
00:35:17,818 --> 00:35:19,479
Hans...

438
00:35:20,863 --> 00:35:23,291
I'm willing to work with you.

439
00:35:24,533 --> 00:35:32,008
So that we can give justice
to Siloy's death and Uncle Edmond's blindness.

440
00:35:32,008 --> 00:35:34,944
How did Uncle Edmond get involved?

441
00:35:37,080 --> 00:35:38,577
What do you know?

442
00:35:43,720 --> 00:35:46,055
Come to think of it, Liam,

443
00:35:46,055 --> 00:35:51,427
when Joyce told me
that Uncle Edmond knew the suspect,

444
00:35:51,427 --> 00:35:57,410
he overdosed before I could talk to him.

445
00:35:59,869 --> 00:36:02,304
What do you think?

446
00:36:02,304 --> 00:36:03,873
Was there foul play?

447
00:36:03,873 --> 00:36:07,387
That what happened to Uncle Edmond
was not self-inflicted?

448
00:36:26,662 --> 00:36:29,031
Thank goodness.

449
00:36:29,031 --> 00:36:31,333
There he is.

450
00:36:31,333 --> 00:36:35,709
Your father has been waiting for you, son.

451
00:36:38,670 --> 00:36:40,843
He even brought cake.

452
00:36:40,843 --> 00:36:42,826
But I'm on a diet.

453
00:36:44,914 --> 00:36:46,916
That's not for you.

454
00:36:46,916 --> 00:36:49,351
I brought it for Liam.

455
00:36:49,351 --> 00:36:52,221
I dropped by to congratulate you.

456
00:36:52,221 --> 00:36:55,558
Your movie is so successful.

457
00:36:55,558 --> 00:36:57,805
I'm so proud of you.

458
00:36:59,093 --> 00:37:03,898
Of course, you're proud,
because the film is making profits.

459
00:37:03,898 --> 00:37:06,890
You think about nothing else but money.

460
00:37:08,904 --> 00:37:13,642
Is that how your mother talks to you, too?

461
00:37:13,642 --> 00:37:15,945
We have lots of vacant rooms at home.

462
00:37:15,945 --> 00:37:18,047
You might want to move in.

463
00:37:18,047 --> 00:37:21,683
My son is not coming with you.
I'll kill if I have to.

464
00:37:23,586 --> 00:37:26,822
I've been telling your father to leave.

465
00:37:26,822 --> 00:37:32,294
I told him to go to Casa Fuerte
so he could talk to you.

466
00:37:32,294 --> 00:37:34,130
He said he would wait for you.

467
00:37:34,130 --> 00:37:35,231
Look.

468
00:37:35,231 --> 00:37:36,432
Why?

469
00:37:36,432 --> 00:37:39,441
What if I want to see you, too?

470
00:37:39,441 --> 00:37:40,855
Whatever.

471
00:37:41,570 --> 00:37:43,939
I'm leaving.

472
00:37:43,939 --> 00:37:45,840
I'll take this cake.

473
00:37:52,933 --> 00:37:54,207
Dad.

474
00:37:59,955 --> 00:38:04,434
I know I already asked you this...

475
00:38:05,861 --> 00:38:08,673
But please tell me the truth.

476
00:38:10,633 --> 00:38:14,839
What do you know about Siloy's death?

477
00:38:16,272 --> 00:38:19,942
And about Lando,
the Congressman's right-hand man?

478
00:38:19,942 --> 00:38:22,595
Are you still working with them?

479
00:38:24,713 --> 00:38:27,658
Can you not ask me such questions?

480
00:38:29,451 --> 00:38:32,655
Ramon already set me free.

481
00:38:32,655 --> 00:38:36,383
I will no longer work for him.

482
00:38:36,383 --> 00:38:40,821
He even let go of Casa Fuerte and Blacksmith.

483
00:38:42,364 --> 00:38:45,134
Ramon will run for Senator.

484
00:38:45,134 --> 00:38:50,345
So the money he makes in our companies
is no longer enough.

485
00:38:54,376 --> 00:38:57,646
Our companies are already free.

486
00:38:57,646 --> 00:39:02,284
Vergil is now the CEO of Casa Fuerte.

487
00:39:02,284 --> 00:39:09,667
Now, you can make films as much as you want.

488
00:39:27,901 --> 00:39:30,879
[Incoming call: Joyce]

489
00:39:30,879 --> 00:39:32,381
Dad, excuse me.

490
00:39:32,381 --> 00:39:33,797
Okay.

491
00:39:36,018 --> 00:39:38,020
Hello, Joyce.

492
00:39:38,020 --> 00:39:39,922
<i>Liam, where are you?</i>

493
00:39:39,922 --> 00:39:42,398
<i>You're the only one missing here.</i>

494
00:39:46,999 --> 00:39:48,453
Okay.

495
00:39:56,705 --> 00:39:58,187
Liam...

496
00:39:58,991 --> 00:40:02,211
It's time for you to do what's right.

497
00:40:02,211 --> 00:40:05,480
We've lived in sin.

498
00:40:18,160 --> 00:40:20,929
- Congratulations!
- Boss Bro.

499
00:40:20,929 --> 00:40:25,100
Congratulations!

500
00:40:25,100 --> 00:40:27,446
Congrats on our movie's success.

501
00:40:27,446 --> 00:40:29,314
Right?

502
00:40:30,439 --> 00:40:32,441
- Cheers.
- Thank you so much, everyone.

503
00:40:32,441 --> 00:40:39,982
I'm so glad
to see you all happy and complete.

504
00:40:39,982 --> 00:40:42,785
To many more successful projects!

505
00:40:42,785 --> 00:40:45,593
Cheers!

506
00:40:49,491 --> 00:40:51,927
Cheers, Sir!

507
00:40:51,927 --> 00:40:55,631
There's no such thing as a perfect life.

508
00:40:55,631 --> 00:41:00,378
Something challenging and painful
always happens.

509
00:41:01,437 --> 00:41:05,604
I'm slowly accepting
what happened to my father.

510
00:41:07,643 --> 00:41:13,793
Now I can say that I have no regrets.

511
00:41:13,793 --> 00:41:16,369
I know I'm content.

512
00:41:43,679 --> 00:41:45,814
What are we waiting for?

513
00:41:45,814 --> 00:41:47,924
Party, party!

514
00:41:49,651 --> 00:41:51,353
Party, party!

515
00:41:51,353 --> 00:41:53,021
Let's party!

516
00:41:53,021 --> 00:41:54,857
Congratulations!

517
00:41:54,857 --> 00:41:57,659
Of course, congratulations everyone.

518
00:41:57,659 --> 00:41:59,194
Shot, shot, shot.

519
00:41:59,194 --> 00:42:05,200
To all the hardworking staff,
congratulations to you all.

520
00:42:13,108 --> 00:42:14,750
Uncle Edmond.

521
00:42:15,679 --> 00:42:17,311
I know that voice.

522
00:42:17,311 --> 00:42:19,189
Liam.

523
00:42:19,189 --> 00:42:20,337
Yes, Uncle.

524
00:42:20,337 --> 00:42:24,888
One of the things I learned
from what happened to me,

525
00:42:24,888 --> 00:42:26,790
is that there may be things
the eyes can't see,

526
00:42:26,790 --> 00:42:29,062
but the heart will hear it.

527
00:42:30,093 --> 00:42:31,757
You're sad.

528
00:42:35,065 --> 00:42:37,179
No, I'm not.

529
00:42:38,435 --> 00:42:40,601
If you have a problem, don't be shy.

530
00:42:40,601 --> 00:42:43,573
You can come to me. We can talk.

531
00:42:43,573 --> 00:42:45,575
You're like a family to me.

532
00:42:47,177 --> 00:42:49,780
Thank you.

533
00:42:49,780 --> 00:42:53,171
Congratulations on your film.

534
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:57,321
My daughter is content.

535
00:42:57,321 --> 00:43:00,590
A heartfelt thanks to you.

536
00:43:00,590 --> 00:43:03,837
Joyce has fulfilled her dream.

537
00:43:03,837 --> 00:43:06,210
Thank you so much, Uncle.

538
00:43:32,456 --> 00:43:35,058
Great job! Great!

539
00:43:35,058 --> 00:43:36,626
Your voice is great.

540
00:43:36,626 --> 00:43:37,828
It can't just be me.

541
00:43:37,828 --> 00:43:39,663
Boss Bro, please sing for us.

542
00:43:39,663 --> 00:43:41,698
Yes, that's right.

543
00:43:41,698 --> 00:43:45,068
DJ, please play the song "Oras".

544
00:43:45,068 --> 00:43:49,840
It's better if you sing too, girl.

545
00:43:49,840 --> 00:43:52,042
Girl, let's go!

546
00:43:52,042 --> 00:43:53,243
This way.

547
00:43:53,243 --> 00:43:55,380
Let's give them a round of applause!

548
00:43:56,546 --> 00:43:58,582
- You do it.
- You can do it.

549
00:43:58,582 --> 00:43:59,816
- I don't want to sing.
- You can't say no.

550
00:43:59,816 --> 00:44:00,817
- This is embarrassing.
- You're the heroes, right?

551
00:44:00,817 --> 00:44:03,487
You can do it.

552
00:44:03,487 --> 00:44:05,255
Can we do this?

553
00:44:05,255 --> 00:44:07,190
I don't know.

554
00:44:07,190 --> 00:44:08,817
Okay, let's try.

555
00:44:11,261 --> 00:44:13,051
You go first?

556
00:44:14,398 --> 00:44:16,131
Me first?

557
00:44:16,131 --> 00:44:17,989
You can do it.

558
00:44:17,989 --> 00:44:19,936
This is embarrassing.

559
00:44:23,010 --> 00:44:29,310
<i>♫ In our one year together ♫</i>

560
00:44:29,310 --> 00:44:35,985
<i>♫ Everything I dreamed of came true ♫</i>

561
00:44:35,985 --> 00:44:43,259
<i>♫ A whole month seemed to disappear ♫</i>

562
00:44:43,259 --> 00:44:49,296
<i>♫ Whenever I was with you,
oh, how quickly time flew ♫</i>

563
00:44:49,296 --> 00:44:56,423
<i>♫ And if only I could go back to the past ♫</i>

564
00:44:56,423 --> 00:45:03,386
<i>♫ I would make sure I never hurt you ♫</i>

565
00:45:05,510 --> 00:45:11,921
<i>♫ Every day, I regret ♫</i>

566
00:45:11,921 --> 00:45:19,476
<i>♫ Letting things turn out this way ♫</i>

567
00:45:19,476 --> 00:45:25,944
<i>♫ If only I had known
this was where we would end ♫</i>

568
00:45:25,944 --> 00:45:34,687
<i>♫ I would have cherished
every hour I spent with you ♫</i>

569
00:45:38,315 --> 00:45:39,382
Thank you.

570
00:45:39,382 --> 00:45:41,617
My friend is so great!

571
00:45:45,252 --> 00:45:47,952
Guys, hello. Congratulations.

572
00:45:47,952 --> 00:45:49,157
- Babe.
- Odet.

573
00:45:49,157 --> 00:45:50,529
Babe, hello.

574
00:45:50,529 --> 00:45:51,995
Hi, Babe. I thought...

575
00:45:51,995 --> 00:45:53,661
Uncle.

576
00:45:55,543 --> 00:45:58,733
Babe, I thought you couldn't make it.

577
00:45:58,733 --> 00:46:00,601
I finished early.

578
00:46:00,601 --> 00:46:04,038
So, here I am. How are you?
Are you having fun?

579
00:46:05,005 --> 00:46:07,598
Of course. Have you eaten yet?

580
00:46:07,598 --> 00:46:09,043
Not yet. I'm hungry.

581
00:46:09,043 --> 00:46:11,092
Don't worry. I'll fix you a plate.

582
00:46:11,092 --> 00:46:12,893
Okay. Thank you.

583
00:46:18,453 --> 00:46:23,390
Liam... Why aren't you answering my calls?

584
00:46:24,392 --> 00:46:28,328
I thought you are willing to work with me?

585
00:46:28,328 --> 00:46:31,054
You think someone turned Uncle blind, right?

586
00:46:31,054 --> 00:46:33,593
Who is it? Who do you have in mind?

587
00:46:34,969 --> 00:46:37,898
Forget everything I said, Attorney.

588
00:46:39,508 --> 00:46:41,442
I don't know anything.

589
00:46:41,442 --> 00:46:43,911
Everything is fine.

590
00:46:43,911 --> 00:46:45,813
Let's not cause trouble.

591
00:46:45,813 --> 00:46:47,992
- Wait.
- Babe, what...

592
00:47:09,771 --> 00:47:11,606
<i>Joyce. Joyce, hang in there.</i>

593
00:47:11,606 --> 00:47:12,874
<i>Joyce, hang in there, okay?</i>

594
00:47:12,874 --> 00:47:15,343
<i>4:46 AM, time of death.</i>

595
00:47:15,343 --> 00:47:16,344
Liam?

596
00:47:16,344 --> 00:47:18,613
I didn't mean it. Joyce, forgive me.

597
00:47:18,613 --> 00:47:22,383
Liam, what are you doing?
What sin are you talking about?

598
00:47:31,961 --> 00:47:34,449
Liam, what was it that I saw?

599
00:47:41,202 --> 00:47:45,239
You're the man in my dreams.

600
00:47:50,311 --> 00:47:51,878
You're using a typewriter.

601
00:47:51,878 --> 00:47:55,216
There's something you always tell me
in my dreams...

602
00:47:55,216 --> 00:47:57,872
That you did something wrong.

603
00:48:00,821 --> 00:48:03,467
I don't understand. Why is it like that?

604
00:48:03,467 --> 00:48:06,561
Why does it feel like it really happened?

605
00:48:06,561 --> 00:48:10,778
We were shooting a scene in our film,
and then...

606
00:48:10,778 --> 00:48:13,464
I saw I was shot.

607
00:48:14,788 --> 00:48:19,385
I felt that I died.

608
00:48:37,933 --> 00:48:39,427
I saw it. It felt real.

609
00:48:39,427 --> 00:48:42,096
I was shot. I died.
It felt like it really happened.

610
00:48:42,096 --> 00:48:43,865
I died.

611
00:48:43,865 --> 00:48:45,409
Promise me this.

612
00:48:45,409 --> 00:48:47,722
You will protect my daughter.

613
00:48:47,722 --> 00:48:50,573
You might be dealing
with an influential person.

614
00:48:50,573 --> 00:48:52,956
And I don't want my daughter to get involved.

615
00:48:52,956 --> 00:48:54,608
I love your daughter so much.

616
00:48:54,608 --> 00:48:57,011
Rest in power. Stefano Lualhati.

617
00:48:57,011 --> 00:48:57,945
What?

618
00:48:57,945 --> 00:48:59,814
- I can't understand you.
- Liam, what are you doing?

619
00:48:59,814 --> 00:49:01,128
What am I doing?

620
00:49:01,128 --> 00:49:04,385
Tell me, what's happening? Where's Sep?

621
00:49:04,385 --> 00:49:07,320
That night, we heard him screaming.

622
00:49:07,320 --> 00:49:11,810
And when we got out,
we saw him on the road, unconscious.

623
00:49:11,810 --> 00:49:15,162
The surrounding smelled like gasoline.
